#Linux Prompt

ubuntu@ip-10-0-0-31:~$

Meaning
ubuntu      → username
@           → separator
ip-10-0-0-31 → hostname of the server
:~          → current directory (home directory)
$           → normal user

So:

ubuntu@ip-10-0-0-31:~$

means user ubuntu is logged into the server ip-10-0-0-31 and is currently in the home directory.

If you become root

When you run:

sudo -i

the prompt changes to something like:

root@ip-10-0-0-31:~#

Here:

root → administrator user
#    → root/administrator prompt
Important interview point
Prompt	Meaning
ubuntu@ip-10-0-0-31:~$	Ubuntu normal user
root@ip-10-0-0-31:~#	Root user
ubuntu@ip-10-0-0-31:/var/www$	Ubuntu user inside /var/www

$ = normal user
# = root user
